    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), keeping each piece of logic in its proper place:\n\n1. **`util/MembershipNumberFormatter.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility formatter mirroring the existing `CustomerCodeGenerator` style. It computes `\"<customerCode>-M<YY>\"` where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration year (zero-padded), returning `null` if either input is missing.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression so `membershipNumber` is derived from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate` at mapping time, exactly like the sibling read-only fields `displayName` and `initials`. No redundant persisted column.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the new read-only `membershipNumber` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nBecause the number is derived purely from fields already on the owner, it's seed-independent \u2014 matching the acceptance test's expectation (`customerCode + \"-M\" + registrationDate.substring(2,4)`).\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
